WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:18.303
eight o'clock the next morning, we released the small boat from its hiding place atop the Nautilus.

2
00:00:19.003 --> 00:00:20.183
The sea was fairly calm.

3
00:00:21.104 --> 00:00:26.066
With Conseil and me rowing, Ned steered us safely past the coral reef that surrounded the island of

4
00:00:26.106 --> 00:00:29.928
Gilboa. I was overwhelmed at setting foot on land again.

5
00:00:30.896 --> 00:00:35.279
Ned strode across the sand as if he were an explorer taking possession of the island.

6
00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:40.523
It was hard to believe that only two months had passed since we had become "passengers onboard the

7
00:00:40.563 --> 00:00:42.745
Nautilus" in Captain Nemo's words.

8
00:00:43.726 --> 00:00:47.008
In reality we were prisoners of the submarine's commander.

9
00:00:47.929 --> 00:00:50.491
Within a few minutes we had plunged into a deep forest.

10
00:00:51.311 --> 00:00:57.396
While I was impressed by the beautiful mimosa and hibiscus flowers, Ned concentrated on getting something to eat.

11
00:00:58.316 --> 00:01:01.418
He discovered a coconut palm and retrieved some of the fruit.

12
00:01:02.859 --> 00:01:07.142
After he broke open a coconut with his hatchet, we drank the milk and ate the meat with

13
00:01:07.282 --> 00:01:09.163
gusto. "Excellent!"

14
00:01:09.484 --> 00:01:10.104
proclaimed Ned.

15
00:01:10.124 --> 00:01:12.606
"Exquisite!" said Conseil.

16
00:01:12.626 --> 00:01:19.390
"Professor, I don't think that Captain Nemo would object to our bringing some coconuts onboard the Nautilus, do

17
00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:20.351
you?" said Ned.

18
00:01:20.371 --> 00:01:25.975
"I don't think he'd mind," I said, "but he won't taste them because they come from the land."

19
00:01:25.995 --> 00:01:28.704
"Too bad for him," said Conseil.

20
00:01:28.724 --> 00:01:33.727
"And all the better for us because there will be more for us to eat," said Ned.

21
00:01:33.747 --> 00:01:39.211
"I have only one note of caution," I said as Ned began to attack another coconut tree.

22
00:01:39.231 --> 00:01:46.275
"Coconuts are delicious, but before filling our boat with them, let's explore and see if this island produces

23
00:01:46.335 --> 00:01:47.456
any other useful things.

24
00:01:48.997 --> 00:01:52.178
Fresh vegetables would be a welcome addition to our diet onboard the Nautilus."

25
00:01:53.139 --> 00:01:55.312
"You are right," said Conseil.

26
00:01:55.332 --> 00:02:00.675
"I propose that we save three spaces on our little boat: one for fruits, one for vegetables, and

27
00:02:00.735 --> 00:02:01.235
one for meat.

28
00:02:02.256 --> 00:02:06.638
And speaking of meat, I have yet to see even the smallest example of an animal on this

29
00:02:06.738 --> 00:02:10.220
island." "Conseil, you must be patient," said Ned.

30
00:02:11.141 --> 00:02:15.943
For two hours we walked through the forest until we came upon a grove of breadfruit trees.

31
00:02:17.004 --> 00:02:20.926
Ned was familiar with the breadfruit, having eaten it during his numerous voyages.

32
00:02:21.866 --> 00:02:23.547
He became very excited at the sight of it.

33
00:02:25.424 --> 00:02:29.748
"Professor, I will die if I don't taste some of this breadfruit right now," said Ned.

34
00:02:29.768 --> 00:02:32.370
"Taste as much as you want," I said.

35
00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:35.573
"We're here to explore the island and the food it provides."

36
00:02:37.074 --> 00:02:38.915
"It won't take long," Ned promised.

37
00:02:39.836 --> 00:02:43.099
While Conseil and I gathered breadfruit, Ned got a fire going.

38
00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:48.263
Conseil brought a dozen breadfruit to Ned, who cut them into thick slices.

39
00:02:49.344 --> 00:02:52.206
"You will see how good this is, Professor," said Ned.

40
00:02:52.226 --> 00:02:53.928
"Have you ever eaten it before?"

41
00:02:54.952 --> 00:02:55.452
"No, Ned."

42
00:02:56.253 --> 00:02:57.434
I wasn't sure that I would like it.

43
00:02:57.454 --> 00:03:01.316
"Well then, prepare yourself for something delicious.

44
00:03:02.076 --> 00:03:05.358
If you don't come back for more, then I'm no longer the king of the harpooners."

45
00:03:06.379 --> 00:03:10.562
After a few minutes, the part of the fruit that was exposed to the fire was completely roasted.

46
00:03:11.462 --> 00:03:16.185
The interior looked like a white pastry, and I must confess that Ned was right.

47
00:03:17.186 --> 00:03:20.908
It was absolutely delicious, and I ate it with great enthusiasm.

48
00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:27.690
We continued to travel through the forest, gathering bananas, pineapples, beans, and yams.

49
00:03:28.711 --> 00:03:32.192
At five o'clock we loaded our small boat and rowed away from shore.

50
00:03:33.233 --> 00:03:36.414
As we pulled up next to the Nautilus, no one came to greet us.

51
00:03:37.435 --> 00:03:39.076
The black hull seemed deserted.

52
00:03:39.776 --> 00:03:44.238
We loaded our provisions onboard and returned to our cabins, where we found supper waiting.

53
00:03:45.218 --> 00:03:48.780
The next morning there was nothing new onboard, no sign of life.

54
00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:52.702
Our small boat rested where we had left it next to the submarine.

55
00:03:53.762 --> 00:03:55.263
Again we rowed out to the island.

56
00:03:55.984 --> 00:04:00.366
Ned hoped to have better luck with regard to hunting, so we decided to visit another part of

57
00:04:00.406 --> 00:04:00.827
the island.

58
00:04:01.787 --> 00:04:06.990
After crossing a large prairie, we came to a small forest filled with brightly colored birds.

59
00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:11.693
"These are only small birds," said Conseil in a disappointed tone.

60
00:04:11.713 --> 00:04:16.616
"Yes, but they can be eaten if you're hungry enough," said Ned.

61
00:04:17.568 --> 00:04:22.409
We decided to keep walking and soon came across some larger, more beautiful birds.

62
00:04:22.429 --> 00:04:24.410
"Birds of paradise!"

63
00:04:25.190 --> 00:04:28.371
I exclaimed as the birds took off in undulating flight.

64
00:04:29.311 --> 00:04:33.492
We must have used half our ammunition trying to bring one down, but we were unsuccessful.

65
00:04:34.293 --> 00:04:35.293
Hunger drove us on.

66
00:04:36.233 --> 00:04:38.854
Finally Conseil shot two pigeons for our breakfast.

67
00:04:39.554 --> 00:04:42.315
While the birds roasted, Ned prepared some breadfruit.

68
00:04:42.335 --> 00:04:46.616
"These birds are excellent," he said, "but they are only side dishes.

69
00:04:47.516 --> 00:04:49.398
I won't be happy until I get some cutlets."

70
00:04:50.419 --> 00:04:54.642
I knew that I wouldn't be happy until I got a bird of paradise—not to eat but to

71
00:04:54.702 --> 00:04:55.823
keep for my collection.

72
00:04:56.844 --> 00:04:58.526
After eating we continued walking.

73
00:05:00.007 --> 00:05:02.329
Some harmless snakes glided out of our path.

74
00:05:03.029 --> 00:05:07.053
Birds of paradise fled at our approach and I despaired at ever getting one.

75
00:05:08.034 --> 00:05:13.859
But Conseil, who was walking ahead of me, suddenly uttered a cry of triumph and held up a

76
00:05:13.919 --> 00:05:15.100
magnificent specimen.

77
00:05:16.096 --> 00:05:17.537
"Bravo, Conseil!"

78
00:05:17.958 --> 00:05:18.398
I cried.

79
00:05:18.418 --> 00:05:22.922
"If only I could bring this bird back to Paris and display it at the zoo in the

80
00:05:22.942 --> 00:05:23.823
botanical garden.

81
00:05:24.823 --> 00:05:26.385
How did you ever manage to catch it?"

82
00:05:26.405 --> 00:05:30.608
"If you examine the bird, you will see that I don't deserve any credit.

83
00:05:31.529 --> 00:05:36.453
This bird has been eating nutmeg, which has made it quite drunk and easy to catch."

84
00:05:37.454 --> 00:05:41.697
No sooner did I get my wish, than Ned got his: a large hog.

85
00:05:42.598 --> 00:05:47.177
We spent the rest of the day exploring the island, and Ned also managed to shoot some small

86
00:05:47.217 --> 00:05:50.678
kangaroos. By six o'clock we were back at the beach.

87
00:05:52.219 --> 00:05:57.921
Our small boat was still there and the Nautilus looked like a long rock emerging from the waves

88
00:05:58.021 --> 00:05:58.822
two miles away.

89
00:05:59.882 --> 00:06:02.423
Ned quickly got down to the business of preparing supper.

90
00:06:03.444 --> 00:06:07.885
The hog, grilling on the coals, soon scented the air with a delicious smell.

91
00:06:08.806 --> 00:06:09.986
We had an excellent supper.

92
00:06:10.727 --> 00:06:17.062
Besides the hog, we dined on pigeons, breadfruit, mangoes, pineapples, and coconut milk.

93
00:06:18.142 --> 00:06:20.483
"Suppose we don't return to the Nautilus tonight?"

94
00:06:20.824 --> 00:06:21.444
said Conseil.

95
00:06:21.464 --> 00:06:23.745
"Suppose we never return?"

96
00:06:24.185 --> 00:06:24.666
added Ned.

97
00:06:25.566 --> 00:06:29.668
Just then a stone fell at our feet and cut short the conversation.

98
00:06:30.489 --> 00:06:33.190
My hand stopped in the midst of putting food into my mouth.

99
00:06:34.151 --> 00:06:38.553
We scanned the edge of the forest without moving but didn't see anything.

100
00:06:39.654 --> 00:06:45.540
"Stones don't fall from the sky unless they're meteorites," observed Conseil.

101
00:06:45.560 --> 00:06:49.401
A second stone knocked the pigeon's leg from Conseil's hand, proving him right.

102
00:06:50.421 --> 00:06:53.862
All three of us stood up and shouldered our guns, ready to answer any attack.

103
00:06:53.882 --> 00:06:56.223
"Maybe it was just an ape?"

104
00:06:56.683 --> 00:06:57.363
suggested Ned.

105
00:06:57.383 --> 00:06:59.064
"No, look."

106
00:06:59.804 --> 00:07:01.164
Conseil pointed toward the woods.

107
00:07:01.945 --> 00:07:08.727
"Natives." About twenty natives, armed with slingshots and bows and arrows, appeared on the edge of the woods.

108
00:07:09.667 --> 00:07:11.727
They were only about a hundred feet from us.

109
00:07:11.747 --> 00:07:13.108
"To the boat!"

110
00:07:13.408 --> 00:07:13.768
I cried.

111
00:07:14.644 --> 00:07:16.367
Our boat was moored about sixty feet away.

112
00:07:16.988 --> 00:07:21.496
We started running as fast as we could while stones and arrows fell thickly around us.
